Z||000000||Philphine||07-29-2000||09:37 AM||||<BR>this latest fiero i got, '84, has a 4 speed tranny. since ive yet to get it running (maybe this weekend, i've got 2 whole days off, in a row too) i just kind of rowed it through the gears. i wasn't able to get it into reverse. i thought i'd heard that '84 4speeds were hard to get into reverse. potential problem, or do i need to get it running to know for sure?<P>also, how do i find out if it is one with the 4:10 gear ratio?<P>thanks for any help.<P>sorry posted then realised i wasn't in the tech section.<P>[This message has been edited by Philphine (edited 07-29-2000).]<p>[This message has been edited by Philphine (edited 07-29-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||Gold-86SE||07-29-2000||12:17 PM||||<BR>Look on the RPO Code list in the front compartment on the left front fender. An M19 is the 4:10.<P>I have a 84 4:10 and do not have problems with reverse. If you are having problems check and posssibly adjust the linkage connections at the tranny.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Gold-86SE (Fiero Collector)||||reg||1
Z||000002||GT Bastard||07-29-2000||12:53 PM||||Just remember... Don't try to muscle it into reverse.  You have to b*tch slap it to the side and then push it up.  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||stsmithgt||07-29-2000||01:50 PM||||Since the motot isn't running, you didn't mention if you tried rolling the car forward and back a little to turn the gears a little to help them mesh while the engine is off.  Sometimes sitting still, gears are just sitting in the wrong spot for it to synchro together. (My 2 cents deposited in the forum ching ching!) <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000004||batboy||07-29-2000||03:05 PM||||Yes, high mileage four speed shifters do get a little sloppy. It's usually the nylon shift cables bushings at the engine. I believe Rodney Dickman sells improved replacements for this. There is a fair amount of adjustment that can be done too. Of course, worse case is that the tranny is shot.<p>[This message has been edited by batboy (edited 07-29-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Philphine||07-30-2000||09:29 PM||||ok, i think the 4 speed has a shorter throw than my 5 speed izuzu. gt, i did my best mack daddy imitation and put in gear. it may have been working all along. it occured to me to try to push the car and i couldn't. so i guess it's working. still need to get it started to know for sure.<P>also found out it has the 4:10 gear and ws6 package. also looked at the owners manual thats been laying on the passenger side floor and found the original window sticker. i guess if i were a collector/restorer it would be more valuable, but i'm hoping to make that paper compleatly wrong eventually.<P>still fighting with engine so i'll switch to the tech section where i should have been for this anyway.||||reg||1
